"""Regenerate Rev03 report paragraphs/tables from the system calculation."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,csv,re
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;D=R/'data';T=R/'source'
q=json.loads((D/'system_design_results_rev03.json').read_text())
def replace_paragraph(s,start,new):
    pattern=re.escape(start)+r'[^\n]*'
    out,n=re.subn(pattern,lambda m:new,s,count=1)
    assert n==1,start
    return out

p=T/'task1.tex';s=p.read_text()
s=s.replace('The two LV sections operate independently; no bus coupler is provided.',r'The normal-open four-pole bus coupler provides transfer after source isolation and load shedding. Electrical and mechanical interlocking of ACB-A, ACB-B and BC prohibits all three being closed. Break-before-make operation prevents transformer paralleling and backfeed. The 2250 A incoming setting limits transfer to $\sqrt3(380)(2250)/1000=1480.903$ kVA; shed at least 1191.313 kVA from the adopted building demand before transfer. This follows CLP GuideToSupply v10 section 3.')
s=s.replace('with six LV cabinets','with seven LV cabinets').replace('Their clearance envelopes fit without overlap.',r'The seven 1140 mm bays occupy 7980 mm. The added end-mounted BC bay retains 1500 mm front and 990 mm rear aisles, with 3450 mm remaining east of the board. Separately insulated rear links connect BC to both bus sections; final switchboard assembly construction remains a manufacturer verification item. Transformer and HV clearance envelopes remain unchanged.')
s=replace_paragraph(s,'The main schematic connects',r'The main schematic shows two transformer incomers, a normally-open interlocked bus coupler, separate floor and plant feeders, tenant controls and meters, and the customer MET. Each floor has a 400 A frame MCCB set to 320 A. Each tenant has a four-pole MCCB immediately before its CLP meter (GuideToSupply section 7.4): preliminary O1/O2 100 A and O3 125 A, based on the COP215 area demands including the 1.1 factor. The detailed F1/O1 uses the Task 3 demand and a 63 A NSX100H instead. The schematic identifies this exception. Other tenant final circuits are outside the selected-office design scope. The diagram follows the functional relationships in \emph{Electrical Schematic 1}; \emph{Electrical Schematic 2} guides the final DB connections.')
s=s.replace('2500 A frame with MicroLogic 5.0X','2500 A frame with MicroLogic 6.0X LSIG').replace('No transformer parallel operation or bus coupler is provided.',r'The 4P draw-out coupler is also MTZ2 25H1, 2500AF/2250AT, with MicroLogic 5.0X LSI. Main incomers use integrated phase/neutral sensing for ground-fault protection; the sensor arrangement requires CLP acceptance. The customer retains its own electrode, MET and protective bonding. PE remains continuous and no customer N--PE bridge is added.')
s=s.replace('Select MTZ2 16H1, 1600 A, with $I_r=1440$ A.',r'Select MTZ2 16H1, 1600 A, with $I_r=1440$ A, feeding Canalis KTC2500 copper busway. Its 2000 A allowance for 15--33\% third harmonic, further reduced by 0.97 for 40\,$^\circ$C daily-average ambient, gives 1940 A $>1440$ A. The nominal 2500 A busway rating must not be confused with the riser protective-device frame.')
s=replace_paragraph(s,'To cover initial motor contribution',r'Treat the entire 655.55 A plant/public envelope in each section as rotating load, with initial contribution eight times rated current. Normal operation gives $46.424+8(655.55)/1000=51.669$ kA. During non-parallel transfer both plant groups may remain connected, so use the larger bound $46.424+2(8)(655.55)/1000=56.913$ kA. The selected 66 kA ACBs and 70 kA MCCBs exceed this duty. Transformer impedance, motor multiplier and transfer operation are assumptions, not utility measurements. Full short-circuit discrimination is not claimed.')
p.write_text(s)

p=T/'task3.tex';s=p.read_text()
s=replace_paragraph(s,'The preceding sheet selects',r'The selected tenant is first-floor Office 1. MS-O1 is a 4P4D ComPacT NSX100H TM63D MCCB immediately before the CLP meter, providing isolation and 63 A protection. The 4C35 mm$^2$ PVC copper feeder has CPC16 mm$^2$. Its 28.5119 m plan route plus 3 m vertical/meter-tail allowance gives 31.5119 m from MS-O1 through the meter to DB-O1. Assumed Method B, 40\,$^\circ$C, separate containment and 15--33\% third harmonic give $I_z=99(0.87)(1)(0.86)=74.0718$ A; $48.6<63<74.0718$. The 25 mm$^2$ alternative gives only 59.856 A. The full-size neutral and its loading limit are retained.')
s=replace_paragraph(s,'To bound the phase-neutral voltage drop',r'The phase-neutral feeder bound uses $(2/\sqrt3)(1.10)=1.270170592$ mV/A/m: 1.945239 V at the 48.600 A design-demand/neutral-current envelope, and 2.521606 V in the separate 63 A stress check. The upstream drop is calculated from the stated busway model below; the previous arbitrary 2.2 V allowance is superseded.')
s=replace_paragraph(s,'The voltage-drop calculation sums',r'The origin is the customer main incomer outgoing terminals. Adopt a maximum 28 m developed MSB-to-F1 busway route (design allowance, not surveyed height), with phase fundamental current 1374.458 A and neutral fundamental current at most 10\% of that value. KTC2500 has hot $Z=0.021$ m$\Omega$/m. Allow 10\% impedance tolerance and 0.05 V for internal links/connections: $\Delta V_{up}=1374.458(1.10)(0.000021)(28)(1.10)+0.05=1.027900$ V. Meter tails are already included in the feeder allowance. The distribution segment is $(1.027900+1.945239)/220=1.3514\%<1.5\%$. Worst final drop is $1.936871/220=0.8804\%<2.5\%$. These classroom allocations are checked at design demand; the separate 63 A feeder stress check remains below the 4\% total limit. Harmonic voltage distortion is outside this fundamental-frequency calculation; the assumed phase balance must be maintained.')
s=replace_paragraph(s,'Fault-protection checks assume',r'For minimum earth-fault current, adopt TN-S and an origin external-loop acceptance limit of 0.18 $\Omega$; this is not a measured value. The busway hot phase--PE resistance/reactance are 0.282/0.170 m$\Omega$/m (Canalis table, printed p.143). A conservative $R+X$ envelope gives $(0.282+0.170)(28)(1.1)/1000+0.002=0.015922$ $\Omega$, including connections. Hence $Z_e$ at MS-O1 is 0.195922 $\Omega$, and adding the feeder 0.064129 $\Omega$ gives 0.260051 $\Omega$ at DB-O1. Final-circuit checks retain hot conductor paths, minimum voltage factor 0.95 and B10/B32 reference limits of 4.17/1.31 $\Omega$. Uniform ring paths use the conservative quarter-circumference bound.')
v={r['circuit_id']:r for r in csv.DictReader((D/'voltage_drop_rev03.csv').open())}
f=list(csv.DictReader((D/'fault_protection_results.csv').open()))
table=r'\begin{longtable}{lrrrrr}\toprule'+'\n'+r'Circuit & Out drop V & Total drop \% & $Z_s$ ohm & Min fault A & $Z_s$ limit ohm\\\midrule\endhead'+'\n'
for row in f:
    cid=row['circuit_id'];z=q['Ze_at_DB_upper_ohm']+float(row['Zloop_70C_bound_ohm']);lim=4.17 if row['In_A']=='10' else 1.31
    table+=f"{cid} & {float(v[cid]['final_V']):.3f} & {float(v[cid]['total_design_percent']):.3f} & {z:.3f} & {209/z:.1f} & {lim:.2f} \\\\\n"
table+=r'\bottomrule\end{longtable}'
start=s.index(r'\begin{longtable}{lrrrrr}');end=s.index(r'\bottomrule\end{longtable}',start)+len(r'\bottomrule\end{longtable}')
s=s[:start]+table+s[end:]
s=replace_paragraph(s,'Under the adopted conditions, all 15',r'All 15 design-demand voltage checks pass; the maximum is 2.232\%. Using 63 A for the feeder instead gives a maximum full-path stress bound of 2.494\%. Final-circuit minimum fault currents exceed $5I_n$. For TM63D, the manufacturer magnetic setting is 500 A; allowing +20\% gives 600 A. The incoming minimum earth-fault current is $209/0.260051=803.69$ A $>600$ A; the TM63D curve (DOCA0187EN-04 p.235) gives instantaneous-region disconnection, conservatively below 0.1 s. This replaces the former C63 reference-table test.')
s=s.replace('Additionally, the main protection and RCBOs must have a breaking capacity of 10 kA.',r'The incoming NSX100H is rated 70 kA; final RCBOs have 10 kA standalone ratings plus the documented NSX100H backup combination below.')
s=s.replace('Incoming C63 total energy','Incoming NSX100H TM63D total energy')
s=s.replace('With a reference interruption rating of 6 kA, the fuse meets the assumed PFC of at most 6 kA.',r'The actual point-fault calculation gives a maximum 5.147 kA at FB09, below the 6 kA fuse interruption rating; it includes incoming and branch resistance up to the FCU, without credit for the downstream spur.')
s=s.replace('Main incomers & Schneider MasterPact MTZ2 25H1, four-pole; MicroLogic 5.0X','Main incomers & Schneider MasterPact MTZ2 25H1, four-pole draw-out; MicroLogic 6.0X LSIG')
s=s.replace('MS-O1 & Schneider Acti9 iC60H A9F54463 & C63; four-pole; 10 kA Icn', 'MS-O1 & Schneider ComPacT NSX100H C10H4TM063 & TM63D; 4P4D; 63 A; 70 kA Icu/Ics')
s=s.replace(r'\subsection*{References}',r'\input{system_protection_rev03.tex}'+'\n'+r'\subsection*{References}')
s=s.replace(r'\href{https://eshop.se.com/ae/acti9-ic60h-4p-63a-c-miniature-circuit-breaker-a9f54463.html}{A9F54463}',r'\href{https://www.se.com/nl/en/product/C10H4TM063/}{C10H4TM063}')
p.write_text(s)

p=T/'main.tex';s=p.read_text().replace('C63 4P','TM63D 4P4D').replace('source C63','source TM63D')
s=replace_paragraph(s,'At 63\\,A, feeder drop',r'At design demand, feeder drop is 1.945239 V. The calculated upstream allowance is 1.027900 V: distribution drop 1.351\%, worst complete path 2.232\%. The 63 A feeder stress case gives 2.494\%, below 4\%. TN-S and origin $Z_e\le0.18\,\Omega$ are declared acceptance conditions; the derived DB loop is 0.260051 $\Omega$. TM63D and final B-curve disconnection checks pass under these conditions. The continuation gives maximum-fault and manufacturer backup checks.')
p.write_text(s)
print('Report source synchronized; compile and visual checks still required.')
